each distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Methods first published in this repository, with the release that introduced them
(see CHANGELOG.md and docs/design/ for dated descriptions):

  - Gated importance sampling for marketing mix models, with Bayes-factor
    selection of carryover and saturation families (0.3.0, 0.5.0)
  - Downside-protected budget planning with support flags (0.4.0)
  - Self-check on simulated copies of a brand, lift-test value by posterior
    reweighting, and the MarketingGraph ontology with its audit (0.5.0)
  - The learning loop with value-of-information experiment choice and budget-neutral
    exploration between indistinguishable channels, graded against known truth;
    conjugate geo pooling with sampled shared curves (1.0.0)
  - Regional curve shapes with partial pooling, sampled with NUTS while each region's
    baseline and effects stay integrated out; regional lift tests as weighted
    observations of an integrated-out effect; sampler diagnostics (R-hat, effective
    sample size, divergences) folded into the inference gate (1.1.0)

